PortageHub: plain OpenGL (glow) as a fallback when wgpu cannot open a window.

The live CD runs in virtual machines and on graphics hardware without a working Vulkan
driver; wgpu then fails with FailedToCreateSurfaceForAnyBackend and no window opens.
eframe's glow feature is added next to wgpu (all its crates are already in Cargo.lock and
are vendored; the lock gains only the eframe -> glow edge). PORTAGEHUB_RENDERER=auto (the
default) tries wgpu and, when no window opens within 20 s and a display exists, restarts
itself once with glow; wgpu or glow pin one renderer and never fall back. A failed window
prints the reason and both remedies (WGPU_BACKEND=gl, PORTAGEHUB_RENDERER=glow).
Not upstream; carried from the live CD fork (commits afbd819 and 77f6b61).

